{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:26:15.048Z","data":{"text":"Done. Implemented the atomic read-model rebuild and verified it.\n\n- Added `model/replace.rs` with `replace_read_model`: rebuild file at `<db>.rebuild`, one connection + one transaction, rename only on success, cleanup on any failure.\n- Routed `write_read_model` and `build_read_model` through it; labels, history, manual edits and ownership are all read before the database is touched, and all tables are filled in one fill.\n- Changed `apply_labels` and `insert_manual_edits` to take the transaction; `write_task_outcomes` kept its public signature and shares the row insert.\n- Added `tests/read_model_atomic.rs` covering all four scenarios.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-storage --test read_model_atomic` — 4 passed\n- Full storage tests — passed\n- `cargo clippy -p osq-kernel-storage --all-targets -- -D warnings` — clean\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` — passed\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/226-rust-storage-hardening/.run/results/1.md`."}}
